<%#
  The one button that signs anybody in: (mark) Continue with Vesopa.

  The wording is the owner's, chosen over "Login with Vesopa" and used to the
  letter by every Vesopa product, because a sign-in button's whole job is
  being recognised without being read. The mark is the same white tile the
  Gift console draws, so it reads the same on a lime button, a dark one and a
  ghost one.

  `rel="external"` keeps the no-reload router off it: the link leaves for
  auth.vesopa.com, and that hand-off is the browser's to make — the loading
  bar still shows for it.

  Options:
    href    where to start (default /auth/vesopa/start)
    cls     button classes (default a full-width large primary button)
    label   the words (default "Continue with Vesopa" — think twice)

  The words are translated; the NAME is not. "Vesopa দিয়ে চালিয়ে যান" keeps
  the one thing the button is recognised by in the script it is recognised
  in, on a page where everything around it is Bangla.
%>
<%
  const vbHref = typeof href !== 'undefined' && href ? href : '/auth/vesopa/start';
  const vbClass = typeof cls !== 'undefined' && cls ? cls : 'btn btn-block btn-lg';
  const vbLabel = typeof label !== 'undefined' && label ? label : t('Continue with Vesopa');
%>
<a class="<%= vbClass %> btn-vesopa" href="<%= vbHref %>" rel="external">
  <svg class="btn-vesopa-mark" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="20" height="20" rx="5" fill="#ffffff"/><g transform="translate(3 5) scale(0.14)"><path fill="#a5c715" d="M0,0 L22.7,0 L50.7,49 L77.3,0 L100,0 L62,70 L40,70 Z"/><path fill="#111111" d="M58.3,35 L81,35 L62,70 L40,70 L50.7,49 Z"/></g></svg>
  <span><%= vbLabel %></span>
</a>
